You aren't making a fair comparison.

The game of chess is governed by a well-defined set of official
rules.  Those rules cover everything from player behavior, time, the
size of the pieces, the size of the board, &c.  Even minutiae is
covered.  If a player wishes to adjust a piece on the board, he must
first inform his opponent of his intent.  A player failing to do so is
required, by rule, to make a legal move with the first piece he
touched.

If I recall correctly (it has been years since I've played a game of
chess, let alone studied the rules), use of outside reference material
is prohibited.

